  "reduction": "Hot H2O (POKAZATEL, R08.T4.f), from its hand-over; every profile less its value at the 25 cm-1 cut-off, the continuum's convention (Clough, Kneizys and Davies 1989), as R08.T4.d's H2O table's lines (decision-r08-t4d-kdist.md section 6.4), nodes whose half-width passes 2.5 cm-1 estimated. Each 1 nm vacuum cell's absorption at each node from super-lines: every line's S(T) (ExoMol's intensity formula, Q(T) from the list's .pf, times the isotopologue's natural abundance) binned linearly on a wavenumber grid of a twelfth of the Doppler half-width at 13100 cm-1 (the heaviest isotopologue's where a table takes several), finer than a tenth of the narrowest Voigt half-width; at each node the bins over the cell and 25 cm-1 each side, coarsened by a whole factor while the step stays under a tenth of the node's narrowest Voigt half-width and a 600th of the cut-off (0.042 cm-1), their binning's response divided out, and convolved by FFT with Voigt profiles (Humlicek 1982) cut off 25 cm-1 from each bin at every pressure, at the Doppler widths of the cell's two edges blended linearly in wavenumber; sampled at the cell's points as R08.T4.d's lines are. Every line takes the list's default air width (cm-1 per bar at 296 K, ExoMol's unit), estimated, so that every node's line shape is estimated; sorted into its k-distribution and reduced to two-point Gauss-Legendre g-intervals shared by every node of the cell, by bisection to 8e-4 in T over every column; temperature nodes on E1' (decision-r08-t4e-budget section 1.4: 50 K steps to 1000 K, then each step the largest multiple of 50 K within 10% of its lower node) from the species' floor (decision-r08-t4ef-storage section 1.4, E2), refined by bisection to a quarter of E1's step where the chain test (cubic in T on ln sigma, the client's rows at the standard pressures each read between the table's nodes, the read cubic in ln p on tau) fails 2e-3 within its columns (the gated column, and the species' own Rayleigh column, R08.T4.g's ruling); alternate pressure nodes below 1 MPa dropped where it passes (E3), and an 8-a-decade midpoint added between two held rows below 1 MPa where it fails by the read itself (decision-r08-t4e-unsold's follow-up); ln sigma stored in 16 bits a value (decision-r08-t4d-kdist.md; decision-r08-t4d-kdist-chain.md). Hands over from R08.T4.d's HITRAN2024 table at 300 K, its first node at or above HITRAN's 296 K: at and below 300 K the client reads R08.T4.d's table, above it this one (kDistribution.ts's tableAt). There, at 10 Pa, the 82 cells above a hundredth of that table's peak agree in mean to a median 1.012 (0.68-1.17; over 680-760 nm 1.027 summed), and over the columns at which R08.T4.d's table transmits 0.2-0.8 a cell's transmittance steps by up to 0.096 at 1 kPa and 0.104 at 0.1 MPa in them (hotLines.test.ts). Below 500 nm, where both tables' cells are at most 3.3e-3 of the peak, POKAZATEL's lines sum to 0.48 (380-420 nm), 0.80 (420-460 nm) and 0.68 (460-500 nm) times HITRAN2024's, 0.05-4.1 cell by cell, and a transmittance steps by up to 0.55 at 1 kPa and 0.60 at 0.1 MPa: the lists disagree on water's weak blue lines, and which is nearer the measurements is not settled here. Both tables subtract each line's value at the 25 cm-1 cut-off, the continuum's convention, so that CKD's continuum, drawn at every temperature, is not counted twice (decision-r08-t4d-kdist.md section 6.4). POKAZATEL holds 1H2-16O alone, so HITRAN2024's H2-18O, H2-17O and HDO (0.27% of its abundances) are left out above 300 K. Every line takes the list's default width, 0.07 cm-1 per bar with n = 0.5 (its .def), estimated, and the table holds no self width (R08.T4.d's gives self 4.87 times air): H2O being dipolar (kDistribution.ts's DIPOLAR_BROADENERS), any share of it leaves this table's lines estimated, a steam atmosphere's taking air's width. Against the pending bound it replaces (ExoMol's cross-section service over the same list, per molecule of 1H2-16O, rounded up), the direct sums' cell means are 0.995-0.996 times it at the median at 1000, 3000 and 4000 K (the abundance, 0.9973, and the round-up), 0.69-1.43 cell by cell at 1000 K and 0.93-1.05 at 4000 K. Q(T) is the list's .pf (174.5813 at 296 K). Above 4000 K the 4000 K node is held, estimated, POKAZATEL being valid to 6000 K by its .def. Fetched from ExoMol's site, the database's archive holding POKAZATEL's opacities but not its transitions; its states the MARVELised file served on 2026-10-29.",
